From a508d83cb0846548912b473f8b3e867c57155fa8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: build <build@localhost>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 10:30:50 +0500
Subject: [PATCH] Stack tab switcher: M90 open/close transition and font parity

- The switcher bar fades in over 200 ms (linear) when the stack starts
  showing and fades out over 200 ms from startHiding(), like M90's
  TabSwitcherModeTTPhone (TAB_SWITCHER_MODE_NORMAL_ANIMATION_DURATION_MS).
  On exit the card's composited toolbar now crossfades into the bar's
  place instead of being covered by an opaque bar that then disappears
  in one frame. The bar ignores clicks while it fades out.
- The static tab position on enter/exit (and the toolbar line-up
  offset) uses the browser controls content offset again, as in M90,
  instead of our bar height. The bar also covers the status bar, which
  the compositor does not draw under, so the exiting card landed 63 px
  (the status bar inset) too low and jumped up at doneHiding.
- Bar label 14sp medium (TextMediumThick, M90's tab_switcher_toolbar)
  instead of 16sp; card titles 13sp on phones via
  compositor_tab_title_text_size (14sp on sw600dp, unchanged there).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
